            "review_text": "needlehill\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam454 contributions\n0\nHumble, consistent + opens late\nJun 2016 • Couples\nRed Tomato is our usual option for dinner when it's late and we don't want to cook.\nThis is nothing fantastic; it's hard to qualify the restaurant, as you can have pasta, fajitas, salads, pork ribs, pizzas... A lot of choices. We haven't tried everything but we have our favorites and have been there repeatedly for years.\nFrom my experience, nothing is bad, food is quite tasty, and above all, it is very consistent. It is sufficiently rare for non Asian food in Saigon to be underlined.\nAnd I'm saying this from years of eating there. The place has customers every evening, every day. We have seen countless restaurants and other small ventures opening and closing within a few months in this area of Sky Garden. But Red Tomato is still here, and for long I think.\nIf you want to have affordable late dinner and no Korean food, go to red tomato!\nRead more\nWritten June 30, 2016",
